{"id":"bang-yellow-sea-1945-02-10","title":"A small freighter in the Yellow Sea, 10 February 1945","short":"10 February 1945","eyebrow":"East China and Yellow Seas · BANG's fifth war patrol, in Wolfpack 23 with SPADEFISH, ATULE and POMPON","theater":"pacific","clock":"","window":{"from":"1945-02-10T02:00Z","to":"1945-02-10T10:00Z"},"gmt":true,"participants":[{"id":"bang","name":"BANG","side":"us","kind":"submarine","hull":"SS-385","co":"Cdr A. R. Gallaher","track":"ss-385-bang/5","sil":"balao","alias":"ss-385-bang","colour":1},{"id":"small-freighter","name":"Small freighter","side":"jp","kind":"cargo","sil":"cargo","note":"As BANG identified it (by sound, 2,400 yards)"}],"places":[{"name":"Yellow Sea","lon":123.5,"lat":36.3},{"name":"Korea","lon":127.0,"lat":36.6,"inset":[127.6,37.4]},{"name":"Shantung","lon":121.6,"lat":36.9,"small":true}],"sections":[{"heading":"","paras":[{"text":"BANG's one torpedo attack of her fifth patrol, as typed on her attack sheet, with her depth log. Times are converted to GMT, with Tokyo time alongside.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Outcome","paras":[{"text":"No Japanese record of this attack has been found yet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Reading the map","paras":[{"text":"Positions are BANG's own dead reckoning and star sights; lines between them are straight, and where she went in between is not recorded. Open circles are ships she sighted, at the target's position. As the clock passes each firing time a red ring pulses at BANG's position; hover a diamond for the attack sheet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Clocks","paras":[{"text":"BANG kept zone I (−9), Tokyo time, for this attack.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"What is missing","paras":[{"text":"No Japanese record of this attack has been found yet. Of the pack, only ATULE was still in the Yellow Sea on 10 February: on the 8th BANG ordered her to cover both their areas until the 11th. SPADEFISH was further north (Port Arthur, 6 Feb) and POMPON had left the area on 31 January after 